From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] advapi32: Open an unhandled reparse point itself for its security.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted
upstream.

Get/SetNamedSecurityInfo on an AF_UNIX socket file work on Windows 10
22H2 (measured with docs/wine-repro/ws2_32-afunix/measure-sd.c,
2026-11-17: GetNamedSecurityInfoA returns its DACL, SetNamedSecurityInfoA
sets one, a client still connects), although CreateFile without
FILE_FLAG_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT fails on it for every access mask with
ERROR_CANT_ACCESS_FILE. So the security functions reach the reparse
point itself. get_security_file opened the file without
FILE_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT and failed with ERROR_CANT_ACCESS_FILE; CodeMeter
(ABB RobotStudio) stops its event server on that.

Limited to what was measured: only when the normal open fails with
STATUS_IO_REPARSE_TAG_NOT_HANDLED is the file opened again with
FILE_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT; symbolic links and mount points, which Wine
follows, behave as before.

--- a/dlls/advapi32/security.c
+++ b/dlls/advapi32/security.c
@@ -180,6 +180,12 @@ static inline DWORD get_security_file( LPCWSTR full_file_name, DWORD access, HAN
     status = NtCreateFile( file, access|SYNCHRONIZE, &attr, &io, NULL, FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS,
                            FILE_SHARE_READ|FILE_SHARE_WRITE|FILE_SHARE_DELETE, FILE_OPEN,
                            FILE_OPEN_FOR_BACKUP_INTENT, NULL, 0 );
+    /* the security of a reparse point that is not followed, such as an
+     * AF_UNIX socket file, is that of the reparse point itself */
+    if (status == STATUS_IO_REPARSE_TAG_NOT_HANDLED)
+        status = NtCreateFile( file, access|SYNCHRONIZE, &attr, &io, NULL, FILE_FLAG_BACKUP_SEMANTICS,
+                               FILE_SHARE_READ|FILE_SHARE_WRITE|FILE_SHARE_DELETE, FILE_OPEN,
+                               FILE_OPEN_FOR_BACKUP_INTENT | FILE_OPEN_REPARSE_POINT, NULL, 0 );
     RtlFreeUnicodeString( &file_nameW );
     return RtlNtStatusToDosError( status );
 }
